<title>ITALY: Italian October industrial output rises 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Italian October industrial output rises 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Statistics Institute ISTAT gave the following provisional figures for industrial</p>
<p>production, year-on-year, in October.</p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION	     Oct 96   Sept 96   Oct 95</p>
<p> Production index (unadjusted)    118.0   110.7    117.8</p>
<p> Yr/yr pct change (unadjusted)    +0.2    -3.0     +7.9</p>
<p> Mnth/mnth pct change (adjusted)  -0.9    +0.4     -0.8</p>
<p> Working days in month		 23	21	 22</p>
<p>Note: (The industrial production index was rebased in January 1994 on 1990 levels, replacing a 1985-based index.)</p>
<p>ISTAT said that taking into account the extra working day in October 1996, industrial production had dropped 3.4 percent year on year in unadjusted terms.</p>
</text>
